# --- ServerKit Docker build context ---
# The context is uploaded to the daemon before any COPY runs, so anything listed
# here is never read, never hashed, and never busts a layer cache. Without this
# file the context is ~750 MB of node_modules/.git/venvs — and the build fails
# outright on the broken symlink at backend/.venv-wsl/lib64.
#
# The Dockerfile needs: frontend/ (sources + package*.json), backend/, VERSION,
# and scripts/install.sh + scripts/install.ps1 (the panel serves those two over
# HTTP for fleet enrollment). Keep this list honest — it read "only frontend,
# backend, VERSION" while the agent installers were being served from disk, and
# that wrong-but-authoritative comment is why nobody noticed they never shipped.
#
# NOTE: do NOT add `!exception` patterns here. A single negation makes Docker
# descend into every excluded directory (a nested file might be re-included),
# which both slows the walk and re-exposes the unreadable .venv-wsl symlink.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Node / frontend build artifacts (npm ci runs inside the builder stage)
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/coverage
frontend/.eslintcache
frontend/.stylelintcache
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# Python virtualenvs — large, host-specific, and .venv-wsl carries a lib64
# symlink that the Windows daemon cannot stat, aborting the context upload.
**/venv
**/.venv
**/.venv-wsl
backend/venv
backend/.venv
backend/.venv-wsl
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.tox
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Local dev state (SQLite DBs, deployed sample apps, captured config)
backend/dev-data
backend/instance

# The test suite runs in CI against the source tree, never inside the image
# (release.yml builds and pushes; it does not `docker run pytest`). Nothing in
# backend/app imports from tests/ — the only references are source comments.
backend/tests

# Secrets / environment — must never end up in an image layer
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Docs and marketing assets are not served by the panel (every docs/*.md
# reference in backend/app is a source comment; manifest_spec_service embeds
# its JSON Schema precisely so validation works without docs/ present).
docs
*.md

# Release artifacts and packaging outputs
dist
packages
*.msi
*.wixpdb

# Go agent (lives in the sibling serverkit-agent repo; never in the panel image)
agent

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
